.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1220:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:641:199:### 9. Provenance integration
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1221:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:642:201:Provenance ([ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md)) is extended:
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1222:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:643:204:- A new field on `Provenance`: `proposal_context: Option<ProposalContext>` carries the trust-gate outcome (`auto_commit | corroboration_commit | proposed | rejected_by_tombstone`) and the gate inputs at commit time. Populated only for Maintenance ability calls that write claims.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1224:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:688:313:Also: trust ledger **warms from prior version** when an agent bumps. Original §6 reset on version bump; that's too aggressive. Instead, start the new version at `α = prior.α × 0.5`, `β = prior.β × 0.5` — half the evidence carries forward, halving the sensitivity to prior behavior while not starting cold. Codex's concern about "prompt-only changes inheriting old trust" is addressed by the v1.4.0 project convention that non-breaking prompt edits bump a minor version (per [ADR-0106](0106-prompt-fingerprinting-and-provider-interface.md)), so the warming applies across both cases.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1225:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:697:353:`corroboration_count` on the claim row becomes a cached denormalization (updated via trigger or on write) for query speed. Provenance of each corroborator is preserved. The trust compiler's corroboration factor reads from this table.
