.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1362:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4746:    15	2. **Ability-output events.** [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) makes every capability a named, versioned ability producing an `AbilityOutput<T>`. Each output is cache-keyed and invalidation-tracked. "This output changed" is a new event class operating at ability-output granularity.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1366:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4877:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-7-plan.md:9:DOS-7 keeps `intelligence_claims` as a durable, append-only commit substrate; it does not derive current truth on demand from Provenance envelopes. The design-review answer is: Provenance envelopes remain the evidence payload, while `intelligence_claims` is the queryable commit log, tombstone gate, trust/feedback target, and per-claim identity layer. Load-bearing ticket lines: "The `intelligence_claims` table is load-bearing for the entire v1.4.0 substrate." "Atomic backfill consolidating **all 9 dismissal/tombstone mechanisms** into `intelligence_claims` rows with `claim_state='tombstoned'`." "No worker drains = no migration. No reconcile pass = no migration complete."
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1367:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4880:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-7-plan.md:25:Child tables: `claim_corroborations` with amendment A fields (`strength`, `reinforcement_count`, `last_reinforced_at`, `data_source`, `source_asof`, `source_mechanism`); `claim_contradictions` with amendment C branch/reconciliation fields; `agent_trust_ledger`; `claim_feedback` with ADR-0123 row shape (`.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:91-106`); and `claim_repair_job` skeleton for `CannotVerify` budgets (`.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:112-118`, `:159-165`).
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1368:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4885:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-7-plan.md:37:Keep the table. Deriving from Provenance envelopes fails the product contract: it cannot enforce a synchronous tombstone PRE-GATE, cannot answer "all claims about subject X" without replaying historical ability outputs, cannot carry user feedback and repair jobs as first-class targets, and cannot preserve 9 legacy dismissal sources under one immutable identity. Provenance becomes `provenance_json` plus source/corroboration rows, not the storage root.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1369:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4892:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-7-plan.md:87:W3-B / DOS-211 Provenance Builder feeds `source_asof`, `SubjectRef`, and Provenance warnings. W4 / DOS-5 Trust Compiler consumes `claim_corroborations.strength`, `claim_feedback`, `agent_trust_ledger`, and trust columns; W3-C does not implement Trust Compiler.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1370:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4926:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-299-plan.md:61:Intelligence Loop check: `source_asof` feeds trust freshness and suppression/tombstone resurrection, not direct signals; it can influence health only through Trust Compiler consumers; it belongs in prep/intel context only as provenance metadata; briefing callouts should consume claim/trust state, not raw timestamp heuristics; user feedback remains claim-level.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1371:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4954:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-294-plan.md:61:Do not log claim text, corrected text, notes, source excerpts, or customer names. Activity/signal rows use user-readable but bounded labels and ids; raw text stays in `claim_feedback.note` / corrected claim payload behind normal local data protections. `SurfaceInappropriate` is a privacy/sensitivity signal, not a truth contradiction, so it must not downrank the source or claim.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1372:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4961:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-294-plan.md:89:W3-B supplies `SubjectRef` / provenance source references. `WrongSubject` and `WrongSource` validation must consume those types, not parse ad hoc JSON. W3-G supplies `source_asof`; W3-H supplies claim type registry rules for `NeedsNuance` eligibility. W4 / DOS-5 consumes `claim_feedback`, `agent_trust_ledger`, and trust columns but W3-E owns the per-action semantic map that DOS-5 implements.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1373:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4973:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-211-plan.md:99:W3-E/DOS-294 owns `FeedbackAction` and `claim_feedback`; W3-B can represent feedback as trust contributions by ID, but does not create feedback rows. W3-F/DOS-296 adds `thread_ids: Vec<ThreadId>` with `#[serde(default)]` and no schema-version bump; W3-B must not add `deny_unknown_fields` anywhere that would reject that additive field. W3-G/DOS-299 owns `source_asof` population helpers and semantic bounds; W3-B defines the field and warning carrier. W4-A/DOS-5 consumes the deterministic trust tree; W3-B does not implement numeric trust scoring.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1374:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4983:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:495:204:- A new field on `Provenance`: `proposal_context: Option<ProposalContext>` carries the trust-gate outcome (`auto_commit | corroboration_commit | proposed | rejected_by_tombstone`) and the gate inputs at commit time. Populated only for Maintenance ability calls that write claims.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1375:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4993:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:869:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-7-plan.md:9:DOS-7 keeps `intelligence_claims` as a durable, append-only commit substrate; it does not derive current truth on demand from Provenance envelopes. The design-review answer is: Provenance envelopes remain the evidence payload, while `intelligence_claims` is the queryable commit log, tombstone gate, trust/feedback target, and per-claim identity layer. Load-bearing ticket lines: "The `intelligence_claims` table is load-bearing for the entire v1.4.0 substrate." "Atomic backfill consolidating **all 9 dismissal/tombstone mechanisms** into `intelligence_claims` rows with `claim_state='tombstoned'`." "No worker drains = no migration. No reconcile pass = no migration complete."
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1376:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:4995:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:872:.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-7-plan.md:25:Child tables: `claim_corroborations` with amendment A fields (`strength`, `reinforcement_count`, `last_reinforced_at`, `data_source`, `source_asof`, `source_mechanism`); `claim_contradictions` with amendment C branch/reconciliation fields; `agent_trust_ledger`; `claim_feedback` with ADR-0123 row shape (`.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:91-106`); and `claim_repair_job` skeleton for `CannotVerify` budgets (`.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:112-118`, `:159-165`).
