.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1702:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:7012:.docs/decisions/0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md:48:- Every maintenance ability has a required `test_idempotent` fixture in `src-tauri/tests/abilities/{name}/idempotency.rs`.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1707:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:7040:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:858:.docs/decisions/0126-memory-substrate-invariants.md:10:The v1.4.0 claim substrate (DOS-7 `intelligence_claims`, DOS-5 Trust Compiler, DOS-10 freshness decay, DOS-211 Provenance, DOS-212 DataSource taxonomy, DOS-213 prompt fingerprinting, DOS-263 invalidation_jobs, DOS-265 claim_edges, DOS-280 canonicalization) is large, interlocking, and built by multiple contributors over multiple releases. Without a unifying set of invariants, each contributor independently makes small decisions that drift apart over time. The result: two code paths that could in principle do the same thing end up doing subtly different things, ghost-resurrection bugs re-emerge after they were fixed, and every new feature ends up re-solving the "how do I store this?" problem.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1709:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:7052:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:3097:The v1.4.0 claim substrate (DOS-7 `intelligence_claims`, DOS-5 Trust Compiler, DOS-10 freshness decay, DOS-211 Provenance, DOS-212 DataSource taxonomy, DOS-213 prompt fingerprinting, DOS-263 invalidation_jobs, DOS-265 claim_edges, DOS-280 canonicalization) is large, interlocking, and built by multiple contributors over multiple releases. Without a unifying set of invariants, each contributor independently makes small decisions that drift apart over time. The result: two code paths that could in principle do the same thing end up doing subtly different things, ghost-resurrection bugs re-emerge after they were fixed, and every new feature ends up re-solving the "how do I store this?" problem.
