.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1729:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:7260:   148	`WrongSubject { corrected_to }` is the user-side complement to ADR-0105's `SubjectAttribution` substrate primitive. Behavior:
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1736:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:8492:- Hard depends on W3-B (Provenance envelope / `SourceAttribution` shape), W3-C (claim rows + `claim_corroborations.strength`), W3-G (`source_asof` column + `FreshnessContext`), W3-H (`temporal_scope` + `sensitivity` columns). Read those W3 L0 plans to understand the upstream contracts.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1737:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:8511:- `.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-211-plan.md` — W3-B contract: `SourceAttribution` shape
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1738:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:8512:- `.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-299-plan.md` — W3-G contract: `source_asof`, `FreshnessContext` input
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1741:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:8693:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:3201:.docs/strategy/2026-04-20-v1.4.0-architectural-strategy.md:136:**Every output is provenanced, fingerprinted, and scored.** [ADR-0105](../decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) makes `Provenance` envelope mandatory on every `AbilityOutput<T>` — identity, temporal context, source attribution, composition tree, field-level attribution, trust assessment. [ADR-0106](../decisions/0106-prompt-fingerprinting-and-provider-interface.md) extends the provider interface to return metadata enabling canonical prompt hashing — replay, regression classification, and prompt-vs-input fault isolation all become possible. [ADR-0114](../decisions/0114-scoring-unification.md) consolidates scoring primitives scattered across `signals/bus.rs`, `signals/decay.rs`, `signals/fusion.rs`, and `intelligence/health_scoring.rs` into a single pure-function `scoring::factors` module. Trust Compiler (DOS-5) and health scoring consume the same primitives.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1742:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:8728:   742	| W3-G backfill < 95% coverage on legacy `source_asof` | The 95% bar is in the DoD. If real coverage lands at 90–94%, escalate to founder before relaxing — don't quietly ship at 90%. |
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1743:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:8766:+Algorithm: compute five ADR-0114 R1.4 canonical factor values (`source_reliability`, `freshness_weight`, `corroboration_weight`, `contradiction_penalty`, `user_feedback_weight`), plus composer-local `subject_fit_confidence` and `cross_entity_coherence`. Clamp every factor to `[0.05, 1.0]`, aggregate by weighted geometric mean, clamp final score to `[0, 1]`, then map to `TrustBand::{LikelyCurrent, UseWithCaution, NeedsVerification, Unscored}`. ADR-0114 pins the geometric mean at `.docs/decisions/0114-scoring-unification.md:120-126` and canonical factors at `:290-294`; current scattered primitive code is in `signals/bus.rs:60-100`, `signals/decay.rs:8-29`, and `signals/fusion.rs:31-50`.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1744:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:8768:+Freshness uses W3-G's `source_asof` contract. `ItemSource` already carries `confidence` and `sourced_at` at `src-tauri/src/intelligence/io.rs:29-37`; `effective_confidence()` defaults missing source confidence to `0.5` at `src-tauri/src/intelligence/io.rs:1227-1230`. Trust input prep uses W3-G's fallback chain from ADR-0105 `.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:424-433`, with `FreshnessContext { timestamp_known: bool, ... }`. `unknown_timestamp_penalty` is applied inside `freshness_weight`, not modeled as a factor.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1749:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:8819:+The new risk is scoring a wrong-subject claim as reliable because its source is reliable. W3-B's `SubjectAttribution` fails ambiguous/blocked subject fit for claim-bearing output (`.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-211-plan.md:57-59`), ADR-0123 `WrongSubject` creates per-subject tombstone behavior (`.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:45-54`, `:129-142`), and W4-A additionally downranks `subject_fit_confidence` / `cross_entity_coherence`.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1751:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:8840:+W3-B/DOS-211 provides `SourceAttribution { observed_at, source_asof, evidence_weight, scoring_class }` per `.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-211-plan.md:31-35` and deterministic provenance composition at `:67`. W4-A reads that shape; it does not change provenance schema.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1752:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:8844:+W3-G/DOS-299 owns `source_asof` population and freshness fallback. If W3-G lands first, W4-A imports `FreshnessContext`; if W4-A lands first, define `FreshnessContext { timestamp_known: bool, ... }` under `abilities/trust` and W3-G adopts it. W3-G already plans trust tests for timestamp unknown at `.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-299-plan.md:85-93`.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1755:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:8858:+Unit tests: `trust_geometric_mean_all_floor_05`, `trust_geometric_mean_all_one`, `trust_geometric_mean_mixed_08`, `trust_feedback_boost_clamped_to_ceiling`, `trust_contradiction_present_downranks`, `trust_nan_never_emitted_for_random_factor_tuples`, `trust_factor_count_is_five_canonical_plus_local_helpers`, `freshness_context_timestamp_unknown_applies_penalty`, `freshness_context_timestamp_known_uses_source_asof_age`.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1756:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:8866:+Wave merge-gate artifact: score distribution on representative dev DB, trust math benchmark report, `cargo clippy -- -D warnings && cargo test && pnpm tsc --noEmit` (`CLAUDE.md:20-24`), plus W4 Suite P proof for p99 <5ms and Suite E proof for bundle-1 coherence and bundle-5 correction-resurrection. Suite S contribution is redacted evidence/log assertions for cross-entity footprints and no customer data in fixtures.
