.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2308:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1258:.docs/decisions/0111-surface-independent-ability-invocation.md:183:2. **MCP migration is non-trivial.** Existing MCP tools from [ADR-0027](0027-mcp-dual-mode.md) must be refactored into abilities or retired.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2309:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1290:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:220:ADR-0103 §6 uses these exact field names. There is no `actor_policy` shorthand — the macro attribute names match the struct fields one-to-one.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2310:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1298:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:345:**Nested transactions are forbidden.** A child ability that calls `with_transaction_async` while one is already active returns `Error::NestedTransactionsForbidden` per [ADR-0104](0104-execution-mode-and-mode-aware-services.md) §4. Child abilities that need transactional writes rely on the parent's transaction or are refactored to be invoked outside a transactional scope.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2311:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1315:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:436:6. **Migration stall.** Phase 2 requires holding other capability-level feature work steady for the duration. If product pressure breaks this, the refactor stalls half-complete. Mitigation: v1.4.0 is a dedicated version with no competing feature scope, per the roadmap decision.
