.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2396:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:830:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:8:**Consumed by:** [DOS-7](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-7) (`intelligence_claims.actor` column, tombstones), [DOS-241](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-241) (enrichment refactor design)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2397:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:831:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:15:2. [DOS-7](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-7) elevates `intelligence_claims` to a first-class table with per-claim identity and append-only assertion history.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2398:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:832:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:22:This ADR specifies the actor taxonomy, the propose/commit boundary, the contradiction-handling rules, the agent trust ledger, and the deduplication policy that collectively make humans and agents first-class, equal-structured claim sources. The substrate pieces needed in v1.4.0 are limited: an `actor` column and a `claim_state` column on `intelligence_claims`, plus the propose/commit state machine. The user-facing surfaces (Analysis Inbox, agent trust dashboard, contradiction resolution UI) ship in v1.5.0+ and are out of scope for v1.4.0.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2399:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:833:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:28:Every claim in `intelligence_claims` carries an `actor` string with one of the following canonical shapes. The `actor` column is non-nullable. Provenance's `Actor` type ([ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) §1) uses the same shape.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2400:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:834:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:96:- **Transform abilities** produce `AbilityOutput<ClaimProposal>` — synthesized assertions with full provenance, but no side effect on `intelligence_claims`.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2401:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:838:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:168:Two committed claims at the same `(entity_id, claim_type, field_path)` with different `claim_text` are a contradiction. Contradictions are **never auto-resolved**. Both claims remain in `claim_state = 'committed'` with a contradiction marker:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2402:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:840:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:174:  claim_a_id      TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES intelligence_claims(id),
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2403:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:841:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:175:  claim_b_id      TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES intelligence_claims(id),
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2404:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-300.log:842:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:189:A claim is content-addressed by `dedup_key = hash(entity_id, claim_type, field_path, normalized_claim_text)`. Normalization includes trimming, Unicode normalization, and type-specific canonicalization (e.g., dates to ISO, names to case-folded).
