.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2629:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-7.log:1035:209:[ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md)'s `DataSource` enum is **not** extended with new variants for actors. `DataSource` describes the *origin of information* (Glean downstream, Clay, Gong transcript, user input). `actor` describes *who asserted the claim*. A single agent claim has `actor = 'agent:prepare_meeting:1.3'` and sources `[Glean { downstream: Salesforce }, Glean { downstream: Gong }]`. The two axes are orthogonal and remain so.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2630:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-7.log:1036:215:- `actor` column on `intelligence_claims` with canonical values from §1.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:2637:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-7.log:1061:295:**Consolidation timing — 2026-04-20 update:** Per plan-eng-review AskUserQuestion #1 and the brownfield-as-greenfield founder commitment (D1), consolidation ships in v1.4.0 as a destructive migration alongside the `intelligence_claims` table creation. Original R1.3 deferred consolidation to v1.4.1 out of migration caution; that deferral is retracted. Rationale: at AI velocity + minimal user base, keeping three parallel tombstone mechanisms alive through v1.4.0 creates interop cost that exceeds consolidation cost. The interop is what's expensive; one-table-to-rule-them-all is cleaner.
