.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:3201:.docs/strategy/2026-04-20-v1.4.0-architectural-strategy.md:136:**Every output is provenanced, fingerprinted, and scored.** [ADR-0105](../decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) makes `Provenance` envelope mandatory on every `AbilityOutput<T>` — identity, temporal context, source attribution, composition tree, field-level attribution, trust assessment. [ADR-0106](../decisions/0106-prompt-fingerprinting-and-provider-interface.md) extends the provider interface to return metadata enabling canonical prompt hashing — replay, regression classification, and prompt-vs-input fault isolation all become possible. [ADR-0114](../decisions/0114-scoring-unification.md) consolidates scoring primitives scattered across `signals/bus.rs`, `signals/decay.rs`, `signals/fusion.rs`, and `intelligence/health_scoring.rs` into a single pure-function `scoring::factors` module. Trust Compiler (DOS-5) and health scoring consume the same primitives.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:3319:.docs/strategy/2026-04-20-persona-reviews.md:207:4. `provenance_schema_version` — the Provenance envelope's schema version.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:3407:.docs/architecture/CONSISTENCY.md:63:**Within the invocation.** [ADR-0119](../decisions/0119-runtime-evaluator-pass-for-transform-abilities.md) runtime evaluator pass runs after primary Transform output. If composite < threshold, **single retry** with critique in the same invocation boundary. The retry's output replaces the primary in the returned `AbilityOutput<T>`. No recursion — retry fails → ships with score annotated.
