   102	If MCP tool derivation fails midway, the server must not partially expose unfiltered descriptors. Build the filtered `Vec<Tool>` in a local value, then atomically swap/cache it. If `call_tool` sees a tool name that was listed earlier but is no longer authorized after registry reload, invocation loses and returns an authorization error.
   103	
   104	Rollback is mechanical and migration-free: remove `invoke_ability` from `generate_handler!`, stop constructing bridges, and let current hand-written commands/static MCP tools continue during Phase 2. W1-B universal write fence is honored because W4-C adds no direct write path; all writes remain inside abilities/services and the existing fence (`scripts/check_write_fence_usage.sh:1-22`).
   105	

