     1	# ADR-0107: Source Taxonomy Alignment
     2	
     3	**Status:** Proposed  
     4	**Date:** 2026-04-18  
     5	**Target:** v1.4.0  
     6	**Extends:** [ADR-0098](0098-data-governance-source-aware-lifecycle.md), [ADR-0100](0100-glean-first-intelligence-architecture.md)  
     7	**Supersedes:** The narrow `DataSource` enums implicit in [ADR-0098](0098-data-governance-source-aware-lifecycle.md) and [ADR-0100](0100-glean-first-intelligence-architecture.md); this ADR defines the authoritative taxonomy.  
     8	**Required by:** [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) §4, [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md)
     9	
    10	## Context
    11	
    12	Three ADRs touch source taxonomy:
    13	
    14	- [ADR-0098](0098-data-governance-source-aware-lifecycle.md) defines a `data_source` tag and purge-on-revocation semantics. Its implicit enum is `user, google, glean, clay, ai, co_attendance`.
    15	- [ADR-0100](0100-glean-first-intelligence-architecture.md) introduces `local_enrichment` and describes Glean as a multi-source feeder from Salesforce, Zendesk, Gong, Slack, P2, and org directories.
    16	- [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) §4 references `DataSource` in provenance attribution, including Salesforce and others not in ADR-0098's enum.
    17	
    18	The field naming is also inconsistent: [ADR-0080](0080-signal-intelligence-architecture.md) uses `source`; [ADR-0098](0098-data-governance-source-aware-lifecycle.md) and [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) use `data_source`. Lifecycle behavior per source (purge vs. flag-for-re-enrichment) is also not consistent: [ADR-0098](0098-data-governance-source-aware-lifecycle.md) says AI-generated intelligence is flagged for re-enrichment rather than purged, but downstream consumers (provenance, maintenance audit) had been assumed to purge.
    19	
    20	This ADR defines the authoritative `DataSource` enum, the `SourceIdentifier` extension pattern, the canonical field name, and the per-source lifecycle rules that every provenance-consuming surface honors.
    21	
    22	## Decision
    23	
    24	### 1. Authoritative `DataSource` Enum
    25	
    26	```rust
    27	pub enum DataSource {
    28	    // Direct first-party sources
    29	    User,                    // User-typed, settings, user-written context
    30	    Google,                  // Google Workspace (Gmail, Calendar, Drive)
    31	    
    32	    // Glean as aggregator — individual downstream sources accessed via Glean
    33	    Glean { downstream: GleanDownstream },
    34	    
    35	    // Other direct integrations
    36	    Clay,
    37	    Ai,                      // Local LLM synthesis (not via Glean)
    38	    CoAttendance,            // Co-attendance inference from calendars
    39	    LocalEnrichment,         // Deterministic computation on local data
    40	    
    41	    // Catch-all for future integrations
    42	    Other(SourceName),       // Stable registered name; ADR amendment required to add
    43	}
    44	
    45	pub enum GleanDownstream {
    46	    Salesforce,
    47	    Zendesk,
    48	    Gong,
    49	    Slack,
    50	    P2,
    51	    Wordpress,
    52	    OrgDirectory,
    53	    Documents,               // Generic Glean document results
    54	    Unknown,                 // Glean-reported but downstream not disclosed
    55	}
    56	```
    57	
    58	**Glean is modeled as an aggregator, not as a single source.** When an ability attributes `DataSource::Glean { downstream: Salesforce }`, it captures both the retrieval path (Glean) and the originating source (Salesforce). This preserves ADR-0100's Glean-first posture without erasing downstream lineage needed for trust and lifecycle decisions.
    59	
    60	**Adding a new source requires an ADR amendment.** The `Other(SourceName)` variant exists for forward compatibility but is not the authoring path. New integrations add explicit enum variants via an ADR, keeping the taxonomy discoverable and typed.
    61	
    62	### 2. Canonical Field Naming: `data_source`
    63	
    64	Every place that stores or references a source of truth uses the field name `data_source`. This supersedes [ADR-0080](0080-signal-intelligence-architecture.md)'s `source` field on `SignalEvent`.
    65	
    66	**Migration.** The `source` field on `SignalEvent` is renamed to `data_source` via a schema migration. Existing rows are re-typed in place (the values already map one-to-one with the new enum). The migration is additive-then-breaking: Phase 1 adds `data_source` and backfills from `source`; Phase 2 drops `source`. Both phases land in v1.4.0.
    67	
    68	**Why unify.** Two names for the same concept create drift. Every query, filter, index, and type consumer must know which field to use. One name, one enum, everywhere.
    69	
    70	### 3. `SourceIdentifier` Extensibility
    71	
    72	`SourceIdentifier` from [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) §4 gains variants to match the expanded `DataSource` enum:
    73	
    74	```rust
    75	pub enum SourceIdentifier {
    76	    // First-party
    77	    Signal { signal_id: SignalId },
    78	    Entity { entity_id: EntityId, field: Option<String> },
    79	    EmailThread { thread_id: ThreadId, message_id: Option<MessageId> },
    80	    Meeting { meeting_id: MeetingId },
    81	    Document { document_id: DocumentId, chunk_id: Option<ChunkId> },
    82	    UserEntry { entry_id: ContextEntryId },
    83	    
    84	    // Glean aggregator
    85	    GleanAssessment {
    86	        assessment_id: AssessmentId,
    87	        dimension: Option<String>,
    88	        cited_sources: Vec<GleanCitedSource>,
    89	    },
    90	    
    91	    // Direct provider invocations
    92	    ProviderCompletion { completion_id: String, provider: ProviderKind },
    93	    
    94	    // Glean-cited sources DailyOS cannot locally see
    95	    OpaqueGleanSource {
    96	        downstream: GleanDownstream,
    97	        opaque_ref: String,             // Glean-internal reference
    98	        cited_as_of: DateTime<Utc>,
    99	    },
   100	}
   101	
   102	pub struct GleanCitedSource {
   103	    pub downstream: GleanDownstream,
   104	    pub citation: String,               // Glean-provided citation text or URL
   105	    pub confidence: Option<f32>,
   106	}
   107	```
   108	
   109	**Glean-sourced opaque data attribution.** When Glean returns an assessment derived from content DailyOS has no local visibility into (e.g., a Zendesk ticket the user's Glean account can read but DailyOS cannot), the ability attributes `DataSource::Glean { downstream: Zendesk }` with `SourceIdentifier::OpaqueGleanSource { downstream: Zendesk, opaque_ref, ... }`. Lifecycle of opaque sources is delegated to the user's Glean policy — DailyOS cannot purge data it does not hold, but it can mask or invalidate derived artifacts when the Glean connection is revoked.
   110	
   111	### 4. Scoring vs. Context vs. Reference Classification
   112	
   113	Every `DataSource` variant has a scoring class that determines how it contributes to numeric scoring:
   114	
   115	| DataSource | ScoringClass | Reasoning |
   116	|------------|--------------|-----------|
   117	| `User` | Scoring | User-authored data is authoritative |
   118	| `Google` (Calendar, Gmail metadata) | Scoring | Structured first-party |
   119	| `Glean { downstream: Salesforce }` | Scoring | CRM is the system of record |
   120	| `Glean { downstream: Zendesk }` | Scoring | Support volume is scoring-relevant |
   121	| `Glean { downstream: Gong }` | Scoring | Call data is scoring-relevant |
   122	| `Glean { downstream: Slack }` | Context | Per [ADR-0100](0100-glean-first-intelligence-architecture.md) — context only |
   123	| `Glean { downstream: P2 }` | Context | Per [ADR-0100](0100-glean-first-intelligence-architecture.md) — context only |
   124	| `Glean { downstream: OrgDirectory }` | Scoring | Org structure is factual |
   125	| `Glean { downstream: Documents }` | Reference | Documents cite, don't score directly |
   126	| `Clay` | Scoring | Enrichment data |
   127	| `Ai` | Reference | LLM synthesis is reference material, not direct scoring |
   128	| `CoAttendance` | Scoring | Derived but algorithmic |
   129	| `LocalEnrichment` | Scoring | Deterministic computation |
   130	
   131	The `scoring_class` field on `SourceAttribution` ([ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) §4) is derived from this table, not author-set. Consumers that aggregate sources for scoring filter by class to avoid conflating Slack chatter with Salesforce ARR.
   132	
   133	### 5. Per-Source Lifecycle Behavior
   134	
   135	[ADR-0098](0098-data-governance-source-aware-lifecycle.md)'s lifecycle rules are specified per source class:
   136	
   137	```rust
   138	pub enum LifecycleBehavior {
   139	    /// Destructive purge on source revocation — remove the source rows entirely.
   140	    Purge,
   141	    
   142	    /// Mark the data as derived-from-revoked-source; surface as masked, do not delete.
   143	    Mask,
   144	    
   145	    /// AI/LLM-synthesized content: flag for re-enrichment on next sync, retain until replaced.
   223	Add to the `DataSource` enum:
   224	
   225	```rust
   226	pub enum DataSource {
   227	    // ...existing variants (User, Google, Glean { downstream }, Clay, Ai, CoAttendance, LocalEnrichment, Other(SourceName))...
   228	    /// Backfill-only marker for claims migrated from legacy items that pre-date `ItemSource`
   229	    /// attribution. The underlying source is unknown beyond "DailyOS produced this before
   230	    /// source taxonomy existed." Trust treatment matches `HasSource::effective_confidence`
   231	    /// default (0.5) so backfill preserves existing scoring behavior exactly.
   232	    LegacyUnattributed,
   233	}
   234	```
   235	
   236	### Properties
   237	
   238	- **`ScoringClass`:** `Reference` (most conservative — these claims cannot drive scoring decisions on their own).
   239	- **`LifecycleBehavior`:** `FlagForReEnrichment` (the underlying data is gone; the claim survives until re-enrichment supersedes it with a typed source).
   240	- **Default `confidence`:** `0.5` (matches the legacy `effective_confidence` default).
   241	- **Backfill-only:** new code MUST NOT write `LegacyUnattributed` claims. Production migration is the only legitimate writer. CI lint enforces no `DataSource::LegacyUnattributed` outside `services/migrations/` paths.
   242	
   243	### Lifecycle
   244	
   245	- v1.4.0 spine: backfill writes `LegacyUnattributed` claims for legacy items without `ItemSource`. Trust band parity preserved per DOS-299 acceptance criterion.

